#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128852 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6506f7e3-4c69-5352-a09d-262adee65e59" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Period of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9267ebc3-36a0-58d3-85ab-2687e21151c0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4048" :question/problem "Calculate the period of the function $y = \\cot\\left(2x-\\dfrac\\pi 6\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "Given a function of the form\n\n$$\ny = A\\cot(Bx +C) + D\n$$\n\nthe period is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\pi}{B}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=2$. Therefore, the period is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128853 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fabd8865-cc14-508a-aa81-4ba147f7f8d4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Zeros of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "100740e1-a959-53aa-af58-034a2fc16a8c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4049" :question/problem "Which expression gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x) = \\cot \\left(2x + \\dfrac \\pi 6\\right)$?" :question/worked-solution "The zeros of $y=\\cot x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\cot \\left(2x + \\dfrac \\pi 6\\right)\n$$\n\nwe replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with\n\n$$\n\\left(2x + \\dfrac \\pi 6\\right)\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac \\pi 6 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi\n$$\n\nSolving for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + \\frac{π}{6} &= \\frac{π}{2} + nπ \\\\\n2x &= \\frac{π}{2} + nπ - \\frac{π}{6} \\\\\n2x &= \\frac{π}{3} + nπ \\\\\nx &= \\frac{π}{6} + \\frac{nπ}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} + \\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128854 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8854eaba-96c7-5ea8-a071-7ff7c954f943" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Asymptotes of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c2431212-e58e-52fe-a00b-6f9abfa3589d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4050" :question/problem "What expression gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\tan\\left(2x\\right)$?" :question/worked-solution "The asymptotes of $y=\\tan x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n \\pi\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(2x\\right)\n$$\n\nwe replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $2x$. This gives\n\n$$\n2x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi\n$$\n\nSolving for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x &= \\frac{π}{2} + nπ \\\\\nx &= \\frac{π}{4} + \\frac{nπ}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is\n\n$$\nx= \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + \\dfrac{n\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128855 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd6703d2-36f6-5665-90e3-f75aea5f663b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a General Expression for the Domain of a Transformed Tangent or Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "8faa2f76-decb-545b-b47e-0c37725a34dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4051" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $y=\\tan\\left(\\dfrac x 2\\right)$?" :question/worked-solution "The domain of $y=\\tan x$ is given by the expression\n\n$$\nx \\neq \\dfrac\\pi 2 + n\\pi\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(\\dfrac x 2\\right)\n$$\n\nwe replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac x 2\\right)\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac x 2 \\neq \\dfrac\\pi 2 + n\\pi\n$$\n\nSolving for $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{x}{2} & \\ne \\frac{π}{2} + nπ \\\\ x & \\ne π + 2nπ\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is\n\n$$\nx \\neq \\pi + 2n\\pi\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer."}]}
